# Drafted by Gemini (R11 batch b3), edited. branden_wells's first conversation.

~ start
set branden_wells_met
Narrator: Cedar curls cling to Branden's bright waistcoat as he taps a wooden peg home, humming a warm bass harmony beneath his wife's soprano.
branden_wells [smile]: Evening to you, travellers! Always room by the workbench for another pair of ears, long as you don't mind a bit of sawdust in your hair.
-> menu

~ menu
branden_wells [smile]: Have you come for timber, or just to warm your hands by the glue-pot?
* Ask about his family and the shop -> work
* Ask how the village treats them -> village
* Ask what keeps him worried -> rumour
* [Insight DC 13] Listen to the catch in his voice when he looks at Beatrice -> check_ok | check_fail
* Take our leave -> END

~ work
branden_wells [smile]: Robin and Lark sort the dowels, Jay minds the glue, and little Wren mostly steals the shavings for curls. Give me a tight roof, a full supper pot, and four beds tucked in, and I'm a rich man.
-> menu

~ village
branden_wells [neutral]: Wickermoor's a dark pitch for raising little birds, I won't lie. Still, the neighbours buy our wagons, and Mayor Somerton respects a straight wheel even if we sing with the Brightsingers.
-> menu

~ rumour
branden_wells [weary]: The quarry men brought down a load of ridge timber last week with hare tracks carved deep in the bark. I burned those planks in the stove rather than plane them.
-> menu

~ check_ok
Narrator: His thumb smooths a toy songbird carved from scrap pine, and the cheerful crinkle around his eyes fades as he glances toward the hill.
branden_wells [sad]: Bea stands at the window half the night measuring that crooked roof on the ridge with her callipers. I just want the chapel roofed and our shutters barred before whatever lives up there notices her looking.
-> menu

~ check_fail
branden_wells [smile]: Only a dry throat from singing counter-part since the third chime, friend, nothing a mug of cider won't mend.
-> menu
